# Copy to .env and fill in. This is the only file that differs between machines.
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# .env is deliberately untracked — it holds real credentials, and this repo is
# public. Nothing here may ever be committed with real values in it.
#
# These are used only by local tooling (curl tests, the validator and deployer
# agents). The app itself does NOT read this file.

# --- Supabase (the only backend) ---------------------------------------------
# The URL and the ANON key are safe in a browser and safe to share: row level
# security is what protects the rows, not their secrecy. The app ships with its
# own pair built in (Settings can override them, per device).
PROBEING_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
PROBEING_SUPABASE_ANON=eyJ...

# The SERVICE key is different in kind: it bypasses row level security entirely
# and can read or delete everything. It belongs only in ~/.probeing/, never in a
# file inside this repo. scripts/secret_scan.sh blocks it by value and by shape.
# PROBEING_SUPABASE_SERVICE=  <- deliberately left blank; do not fill this in here

# The GEMINI key is likewise a real secret. It lives in Supabase's own secret
# store, read by an Edge Function — never in the browser, because this repo is
# public and anything the app ships is world-readable.
# GEMINI_API_KEY=  <- set it in Supabase, not here

# --- secrets the `gemini` Edge Function needs, set in Supabase, not here ------
# Supabase dashboard → Edge Functions → Secrets. Named here only so the pair is
# written down somewhere other than a comment inside the function's own source.
#
#   GEMINI_API_KEY     the key above
#   ALLOWED_USER_ID    the one user id allowed to spend it
#   GEMINI_MODEL       optional; overrides the model name baked into the function
#
# GEMINI_MODEL exists because Google retires model names. When it does, the
# function reports the refusal verbatim and names the replacement — set this
# secret to that name and it works again, with no redeploy. (This has already
# happened once: gemini-2.5-flash -> gemini-3.6-flash, 30 Aug 2026.)
#
# ALLOWED_USER_ID is not optional. The function refuses EVERY caller, the owner
# included, until it is set — a 403 saying so. That is deliberate: adding a
# second person must be an act of setting something, never of forgetting to. But
# it means a fresh deploy with the secret missing looks exactly like a broken
# deploy, so check this first when Test Gemini says "not your app".
# ALLOWED_USER_ID=  <- set it in Supabase, not here
